Sup by default, "sup bitches" in his own theme
==============================================

One greeting, two registers, and the boundary is a theme rather than a mood:

* **default** (any theme but his): **Sup**. That is what a stranger meets, and it is what onboarding
  says — onboarding is met by everybody, so it does not get the personal one. It is "Sup" on the
  first-run screen no matter what is selected.
* **the volkdude85 theme**: **Sup bitches** on the welcome screen, with the sub-line to match. He
  chose that theme; it is his name on the build; the register is his.

The persona file carries both, so the spoken greeting agrees with the screen instead of contradicting
it: *"Sup — you're new. I'm Nora. What do I call you?"* by default, *"Sup, bitches — you're new…"* in
his register. Neither is handed to somebody who has not asked for it.

